**Definition 8.5 (complete bills).** For any actual finite prefix let
$n$ count every native row from the irreducible entrance, $A$ count all
constructed nonmeter eight-track cells, and $b_{\rm ctl}$ count the
actual endowed/constructed finite control bits in ARC's convention.
The native tariff is exactly

$$
(\mathrm{ticks},\mathrm{fee},\mathrm{bits})
=(n,2n,S_{\rm irreducible}+b_{\rm ctl}+8A+8n).
$$

All dead banks, bootstrap/capture bits, directory metadata, source
growth, raw partial material, descriptors, staged descriptors, channel
copies, print, import, independent decoders, re-encoding, comparison,
fault cleanup and final return are included in these actual counts.
Only actual emitted rows add receipts; unexecuted disabled attempts do
not. Historical simulation emits represented receipts inside bank data;
its own native simulation work additionally has its own actual receipts.

For the eight full payload lengths
$L_C,L_P,L_I,L_0,\ldots,L_4$, CYCLE Proposition 10.2 gives the disjoint
two-copy-plus-print subtotal

$$
17(L_C+L_P+L_I+L_0+\cdots+L_4)+56
$$

native rows and retained distinct payload material of at least three
times that sum of lengths. These are subtotals, not the full flight.
For a seven-field stage wrapper its exact length is

$$
L_s=29+2\bigl(s+|\mathrm{serviceBinding}|+|\xi|+|b_*|+|v_s|\bigr).
$$

For the separately declared UAS structural tariff, use CYCLE §10.3's
ordered-stencil counts with this actual $q_{\mathrm{gc}}$ and table.
If row $i$ has its listed stencil size $p_i$, let $e_i$ count actual
core-plus-receipt cell births, $s_i$ fresh finite bits, $t_i$ distinct
designated existing native-bit targets after alias combination, $r_i$
head retargets and $a_i$ first activations. Include PC/token/control
targets and prescribed no-op targets as in UAS Definition 4.1; do not
include a freshly constructed bit in $t_i$. Set

$$
\begin{aligned}
v_i&=24e_i+s_i,\\
w_i&=3t_i+2e_i+2s_i+3r_i+2a_i+7v_i,\\
g_i&=1+p_i+w_i+v_i.
\end{aligned}
$$

Use their actual alias combinations and receipt cells as in that source;
these local symbols do not denote the global $a,b$ acquisition bounds.
The full structural replacement account is

$$
\rho_{\mathrm{gc}}+1+8(195+2q_{\mathrm{gc}}+c_0)
+\sum_{i=1}^{n}g_i,
$$

with $c_0$ the initially present finite-slot count. It includes rule
apparatus and the paid initial scaffold/endowment. If both tariffs are
imposed, add the native fee coordinate $2n$ as prescribed there; do
not identify the alternative tariffs or omit the foundation. For
geometric body sizes CYCLE's actual layout count has $C=2+A+n$,
$V=147+2q_{\mathrm{gc}}+c+24C$ and $L=74+q_{\mathrm{gc}}+8C$, with
$c$ the actual number of present finite slots. Thus Lemma 3.3 uses
the actual $c$, not a capacity guess.

Every total can equivalently be obtained by recursively summing the
written native program's executed leaves: sequence adds, the selected
branch contributes its rows, and each actual loop adds its executed
iterations. Expanding all assignments with this $r_{\mathrm{gc}}$ and
all descriptions with this $\delta_{\mathrm{gc}}$ fixes that recurrence.
No numerical execution count or physical benchmark is assumed.

